:: Caught [event mom_quest] {"position":"4150,1075","size":"100,100"}
/* Quest "Caught" (mom_caught), STAGE1_PROPOSAL.md 5.2. Since The Booze Night she has been slipping off to the meeting room
   alone. I walk in on her with her hand under her skirt and the blinds down. I don't let her stop: she finishes in front
   of me, while I watch and don't touch her. Halfway through, $brian.name opens the door to ask me about a part order and
   never looks up. A near miss, and a joke afterwards. Public risk, and the start of his flustered reactions to her. */
<<silent>><<SetBackground $locations[15].img>><</silent>>
It's the third time this week. $mom.callName gets up from her desk with a folder under her arm, tells nobody in particular that she's going to go over the quarterly numbers where it's quiet, and walks to the meeting room. Twenty minutes later she comes back with the same folder, closed, and pink in the face, and she drinks a whole glass of water at the cooler before she sits down.

It's the same folder every time, too. I looked yesterday while she was in there, and it's last month's catering invoices.

Today I give her five minutes. Then I get up, pick up my coffee so I'm a man on his way to the kitchen, and walk the long way round.

<<linkreplace "Open the door">>
The blinds are down on the glass wall. The door isn't locked, because the meeting room doesn't have a lock, because I never thought it needed one.

She's in the chair at the far end of the table, the one facing away from the door, turned a little toward the window. The folder is open in front of her for decoration. Her head is tipped back against the headrest, her eyes are closed, and her right hand is under her skirt. Her left hand is pressed over her mouth.

<<Media "images/characters/mom/events/caught/chair.mp4" 600>>
/* Mom in the meeting room chair, head back, eyes closed, one hand under her pencil skirt, the other over her mouth, blinds down behind her */

She doesn't hear the door. She hears it close.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ text: "Her eyes fly open. The hand comes out from under the skirt so fast that the chair spins half a turn, and she grabs the table to stop it." },
{ who: $mom, text: "Oh my God. Honey, I was just... I was..." },
{ who: $player, text: "Going over the quarterly numbers? That's what you told everybody." },
{ who: $mom, text: "Yes. No. Oh, sweetie, I'm so sorry, I don't know what's gotten into me lately, it's like I'm back in college and I can't sit still for five minutes, and I'll go, I'll go right back to my desk and we never have to..." },
{ text: "She's already tugging her skirt down, already reaching for the folder, already halfway out of the chair." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

<<linkreplace "Sit down">>
<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $player, text: "Sit down, $mom.callName." },
{ text: "She sits. It takes her a second to realize she's done it." },
{ who: $player, text: "You've been coming in here all week, with the whole team sitting on the other side of that glass, and you thought nobody would notice?" },
{ who: $mom, text: "I know, I know, it was stupid and it won't happen again, I promise, I'll just..." },
{ who: $player, text: "I didn't say it had to stop." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

It takes her a moment. I watch her get there: her mouth opens, closes, and her eyes go to the door behind me and back to my face.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $mom, text: "Here? Sweetheart, they're all right out there, $ethan.name is maybe twenty feet from that door..." },
{ who: $player, text: "They were right out there two minutes ago, too, and you didn't seem to mind." },
{ who: $mom, text: "That was different, I was by myself. You'd be... you'd be standing there watching me." },
{ who: $player, text: "I would. I'm not going anywhere." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

I lean against the edge of the table, a few feet from her, and drink my coffee, and wait. I don't touch her, and I don't say anything else to help her along. Honestly, I'm not sure she'll do it. Part of me expects her to grab the folder and walk out past me.

<<linkreplace "Wait">>
She looks at the door one more time. Then she closes her eyes, as if that makes her alone again, and her hand goes back under the skirt.

It's slow at first. Small, careful circles, her knees pressed together, her whole body stiff in the chair. But she was most of the way there before I walked in, and her body remembers that faster than her head does. Her knees drift apart. The skirt rides up her thighs. Her breathing starts to catch.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $mom, text: "Please don't look at me, honey, can you just look at the window or something, just for a..." },
{ who: $player, text: "No. You don't get to hide from me in my own meeting room." },
{ text: "She makes a small sound into her other hand, and her fingers move faster." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

<<Media "images/characters/mom/events/caught/watched.mp4" 600>>
/* Mom in the chair with her knees apart, skirt pushed up, eyes squeezed shut, biting the side of her hand */

<<linkreplace "Someone knocks">>
Two knocks on the door. Then, without waiting, because nobody in this office has ever waited, the handle turns.

$mom.callName freezes so hard I can hear the chair creak. I step sideways, one step, so I'm between the door and the end of the table, and the door opens about a foot.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $brian, text: "Um. Sorry. $ethan.name said you were in here." },
{ text: "He's talking to the floor. He always talks to the floor, and I have never been so grateful for it. His eyes are fixed on a spot about two feet in front of his shoes." },
{ who: $player, text: "I'm here. What's up?" },
{ who: $brian, text: "The emitters. The supplier only has the forty-millimeter ones, and those won't fit the housing. So we change the housing or we wait two weeks. I didn't want to pick without asking." },
{ text: "Behind me I can hear $mom.callName breathing through her nose, very slowly and very carefully. She hasn't taken her hand away. I can tell, because I can hear the fabric." },
{ who: $player, text: "Change the housing. Two weeks is too long." },
{ who: $brian, text: "Okay. Yeah, that's what I'd have done. Thanks. Hi, $mom.callName." },
{ who: $mom, text: "Hi, sweetie." },
{ text: "It comes out sounding nearly normal, which might be the most impressive thing I've ever seen her do." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

He nods at the floor and backs out, and pulls the door shut behind him with exaggerated care, the way you close the door on a sleeping baby.

<<linkreplace "Finish">>
<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $player, text: "Go on. You were nearly there before he knocked." },
{ who: $mom, text: "Honey, he was right there, he almost saw..." },
{ who: $player, text: "He was looking at his shoes the whole time. Finish it, $mom.callName. I'm not going to ask you twice." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

And she does, and it doesn't take long. Whatever that last minute did to her, it didn't put her off, and I suspect that's going to bother her later much more than it bothers her now. She comes with her hand clamped over her mouth and her heels pressed into the carpet and her eyes open, looking straight at me. I never asked her to keep them open. By then she's stopped arguing with anything.

Afterwards she sits very still with her hand in her lap. Then she pulls her skirt down, smooths it twice, and picks up the folder of catering invoices and holds it against her chest.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $mom, text: "I can't believe I just did that, with $brian.name standing right there in the door and you watching me the whole time, what kind of $mom.relation would... oh, God, my lipstick is all over my hand." },
{ who: $player, text: "Relax. $brian.name can barely look at you on a normal day, he wasn't going to start in here. He was too busy saying hi to the carpet." },
{ text: "She laughs. It's a shaky, horrified laugh, the kind that wants to turn into crying and changes its mind. She covers her face with the folder." },
{ who: $mom, text: "Oh, that poor boy, he said hi to me. He stood there and said hi like it was any other afternoon." },
{ who: $player, text: "Go fix your face before somebody else comes looking for me. And next time you want the meeting room, you come and ask me first." },
{ who: $mom, text: "Ask you? Ask you what, honey, how am I supposed to even..." },
{ who: $player, text: "You'll figure out a way to say it." },
{ text: "She nods slowly, as if she's filing it with all the other rules: the one about taking care of me when it gets bad, the one about the test sessions. Then she goes." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

When she walks past $brian.name's desk on the way to the bathroom, he sits up very straight and stares at his monitor and doesn't breathe until she's gone. I don't think he knows why, and I'm certainly not going to be the one who tells him.

<<UpdateStat "+" "MomExhibition" 3>>
<<UpdateStat "-" "MomLust" 30>>
<<UpdateStat "+" "MomCorruption" 4>>
<<UpdateStat "-" "MomResistance" 2>>
<<UpdateStat "+" "Corruption" 2>>
<<Feel $mom "brian" 1>>
<<ProfileLog $mom "Caught" "I walked in on her in the meeting room, with her hand under her skirt and the blinds down. I didn't let her stop. She finished in front of me while $brian.name stood in the doorway asking me about a part order. He never looked up. From now on she asks me before she uses the meeting room.">>
